Subject: [PATCH] Add AdvancedColumnFamilyOptions::blob_dir

Lets blob files be placed on a different volume than the SST files.

Stock RocksDB derives every blob file path from `cf_paths.front().path`, so
blob files always sit alongside the SST files of the first configured path.
`db_paths`/`cf_paths` therefore cannot tier large values: they distribute SST
files by level while every blob file stays put. This adds a per-column-family
`blob_dir` (empty = the historical `cf_paths.front()` behavior) and routes all
blob path derivation through a single `ImmutableCFOptions::GetBlobDir()`
accessor.

Sites updated: blob file creation and reads; directory fsync after ordinary,
atomic, and direct-write flushes, compaction, and WAL recovery (a blob
directory outside cf_paths has no handle in `Directories`, so its entries were
never synced — ColumnFamilyData now owns one); the
obsolete-blob-file path recorded for deletion; the CollectAllDBPaths scan; the
directory created at DB open; both DestroyDB overloads; Env path registration
via GetDbPaths; GetLiveFilesStorageInfo (checkpoint/backup); the column-family
metadata path; full-file checksum verification; the flush/compaction listener
info; and the direct-write blob partition manager, which otherwise writes to
`dbname_` regardless (only overridden when blob_dir is explicitly set, so the
default path is unchanged). Checkpoint/BackupEngine grow a guard rather than a
new path (below).

Checkpoint and BackupEngine refuse a DB with blob_dir set. They already refuse
one whose files span more than one directory (`CreateCustomCheckpoint` checks
`dirs.size() > 1`), and reporting the real blob directory from
GetLiveFilesStorageInfo puts a tiered DB in that category — but only once a
blob file exists to report. Backing one up in the window before that is worse
than flattening: the copied OPTIONS file carries blob_dir, so restoring
elsewhere and opening yields a second DB pointed at the source's blob
directory, whose obsolete-file scan deletes the source's live blob files. So
CreateCustomCheckpoint requests a portable capture through the virtual
GetLiveFilesStorageInfo API. DBImpl tracks blob_dir configuration under its DB
mutex, never clears the flag after a column-family drop, and refuses before
flushing or enumerating files. This keeps the check atomic with the captured
OPTIONS state and works for StackableDB/custom DB implementations without an
unsafe DBImpl downcast. The legacy GetLiveFiles API also refuses because it
cannot report per-file directories. The file-spanning error now names blob_dir
alongside db_paths and cf_paths.

Because a blob file's directory is derived from the option rather than recorded
per file (unlike an SST's MANIFEST path index), the option is immutable and
changing it on a populated DB strands the existing blob files. RocksDB cannot
enforce that without persisting more state, so the constraint is documented
here and enforced by the consumer: @harperfast/rocksdb-js compares the request
against the blob_dir persisted in the OPTIONS file and refuses a mismatching
open. `blob_dir` is deliberately the LAST field of AdvancedColumnFamilyOptions
to limit layout churn within that struct. Adding it still changes the layout of
AdvancedColumnFamilyOptions and its derived option types: every C++ consumer
must rebuild against the patched headers, and binaries compiled against stock
RocksDB headers are not ABI-compatible with this build.

`ROCKSDB_HAS_CF_BLOB_DIR` is defined in advanced_options.h so downstream code
can feature-detect and still compile against an unpatched RocksDB. Version 2
includes the atomic portable-capture guard and complete flush-directory fsync.

Rebase note: authored against v11.8.1 (the version pinned by rocksdb-js).
Re-check the blob path sites on every version bump — 11.8.1 added the
direct-write partition manager, which was a new one.

Downstream-only (HarperFast). Not submitted upstream.
